WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.984
In this video, you will add a whole list of homes to your contest yourself, for example when your city already collects registrations somewhere else.

00:00:08.984 --> 00:00:10.128
We start on the map.

00:00:11.029 --> 00:00:15.091
To begin, open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.091 --> 00:00:17.216
That is the only address you need.

00:00:18.956 --> 00:00:21.363
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:21.363 --> 00:00:25.107
The first time you visit, it asks to use your location.

00:00:25.107 --> 00:00:26.444
Tap Use my location.

00:00:28.185 --> 00:00:32.622
That is how the map shows how far things are, and gives you directions.

00:00:32.622 --> 00:00:35.827
Your browser asks permission as well, so tap Allow.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:40.388
Your location is used only on your device, and you can say no at any time.

00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:46.567
Now look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.762
See the three dots?

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:52.065
That is the menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:52.065 --> 00:00:52.603
Tap them.

00:00:54.205 --> 00:00:56.019
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:57.718 --> 00:00:59.531
Tap Mine, your personal page.

00:01:01.225 --> 00:01:03.294
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:06.225
Now tap Entries.

00:01:06.225 --> 00:01:08.933
Homes can be added here until voting starts.

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:12.240
Open Add homes yourself.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.413
Each home goes straight onto the ballot and the routes, with no photo, and no sign in.

00:01:19.138 --> 00:01:25.364
Paste one home per line: the street address, city and ZIP, then a bar, and the family name.

00:01:25.364 --> 00:01:27.800
The city, ZIP and name are optional.

00:01:28.699 --> 00:01:31.153
Paste your list, up to a hundred at a time.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.515
Tap Check addresses.

00:01:34.515 --> 00:01:37.233
This looks up each address, and adds nothing yet.

00:01:39.313 --> 00:01:40.473
Found means ready.

00:01:40.473 --> 00:01:43.587
Not found means a typo, so fix it and check again.

00:01:43.587 --> 00:01:45.969
Already in means it is in your contest.

00:01:48.155 --> 00:01:53.424
Tick the box to confirm that the residents agreed to have their address shown on the public map.

00:01:55.075 --> 00:01:57.923
The button now says how many homes it will add.

00:01:57.923 --> 00:01:58.872
Tap Add 3 homes.

00:02:01.416 --> 00:02:05.512
The new homes are on the map and the ballot, tagged Added by organizer.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.569
Added one by mistake?

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:09.309
Tap Remove.

00:02:10.984 --> 00:02:12.563
Then tap again to confirm.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.571
That is how you put a whole neighborhood on the ballot.

00:02:17.571 --> 00:02:19.717
Homes can be added until voting starts.

00:02:21.119 --> 00:02:23.892
Next up: Edit your contest and change the dates.
